<Base title="About · Lab Notes" description="A library of AI study outputs.">
  <h1 style="font-size:1.5rem">About</h1>
  <p>
    <strong>Lab Notes</strong> is not a diary of a homelab, and not a class.
    It is a shelf for <strong>study outputs</strong>: pick a topic I want to understand, run it
    through AI research, keep the artifact.
  </p>
  <p>Typical lanes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Deep cut</strong> — Silicon Valley and China labs: models, infra, papers, chips, failures, numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>Scoreboard</strong> — new services; Gemini vs Claude vs ChatGPT vs Grok when it moved.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    English. The point is the file you can re-read, not the author’s journey.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/">← Notes</a></p>
</Base>
